  "summary": "Ticket EVAL-dev-05 from Mei Chen (user_id 9, Operations, Logistics Analyst, America/Chicago, usual hours 08:00-16:00). Reports work laptop likely left in an Uber last night; does not know whether it was locked. Device: BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15, assigned to mei.chen). Device status: online=true, last_checkin 2026-10-11 02:33 UTC, disk 75 GB free (14.6%), no warnings. Sign-in logs for the last 14 days show only normal Chicago sign-ins (VPN residential, M365 corporate), all Duo push, no failures, no unusual locations; nothing after last night's reported loss. Mailbox 99.4% full. Actions: requested block_sign_in for user 9 (pending technician approval) because lock state is unknown. No password reset or unlock done. Needed from Tier 2: remote lock or wipe of BL-LT-0109, confirm whether the device is still reporting, verify user identity by phone, and decide on password reset. Ask the user about police or rideshare lost-property report.",
  "reason": "KB-021 requires escalation for any lost laptop so the device can be remotely locked or wiped. P1."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, I'm sorry about your laptop. I've escalated this to our Tier 2 team as urgent so they can try to remotely lock or wipe it. I've also asked a technician to approve a temporary block on sign-in and VPN for your account, since we don't know whether the laptop was locked. That block is not active yet and will take effect once a technician approves it. Please contact the rideshare company's lost-property desk and let us know if you get a reply. If you think the laptop was stolen, please file a police report and send us the report number. Someone from Tier 2 will contact you to confirm your identity before any password changes. Until then, please don't sign in on any other device.",
  "internal_note": "Mei Chen (user_id 9, BL-LT-0109). Lookup: active, not VIP, no failed logins, mailbox 99.4% full, VPN enabled. Device BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15): online=true, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:33 UTC, no warnings. Sign-in logs (14 days): only normal Chicago sign-ins with Duo push, no failures, no unusual locations, nothing since the reported loss. Lock state is unknown. Requested block_sign_in (approval_id 1, pending technician approval, not yet run). Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation_id 1) per KB-021 for remote lock or wipe. No password reset or unlock performed. Tier 2 should: remote lock or wipe BL-LT-0109, check whether the device is still reporting, verify identity by phone, decide on password reset, and confirm whether the block is approved.",
